# CLI Cheatsheet

## 1. File and Directory Management

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `mkdir -p` | To create nested directories |
| `find -name "*.txt"` | Search by file name |
| `find -type f` | Find all files |
| `find -type d` | Find all directories |
| `find -type f -name "*.log" -delete` | Search all files and search *.log files, -delete |
| `ls -lahtr` | Hidden files, readable sizes, reverse time order respectively |
| `wget "link"` | Is to download its contents in current directory |
| `wget -o name "link"` | Same but download with name as filename |
| `rsync -av project/ backup/` | Copies the contents of project into backup. |

## 2. File Reading and Processing

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `head -n -k` | Displays first k lines |
| `tail -n -k` | Displays last k lines |
| `less` and `more` | Read file page by page |
| `wc` | Count lines, words and bytes respectively |
| `sort -rnu` | Sorts alphabetically reverse, numeric, duplicates sorting respectively |
| `uniq` | Remove adjacent duplicate lines |
| `sed` | Edit text streams if we add -i then it modifies file directly |
| `awk` | |
| `cut` | |
| `xargs` | It takes output and connects to input for another function |

## 3. Text Searching

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `grep` | Search text inside files |
| `grep -i` | Case sensitive |
| `grep -n` | Display line numbers |
| `grep -r` | Search recursively |
| `grep -v` | Non matching lines |
| `grep -o` | Display only matched text |
| `grep -c` | Count matching lines |

## 4. File Permissions and Ownership

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `chmod ugo file.txt` | u-user, g-group, o-others, 4\|r - read, 2\|w - write, 1\|x - execute |
| `chown user:group file.txt` | Change owner and group and -R recursively |

## 5. Redirection and Pipes

| Symbol | Description |
|---|---|
| `\|` | Sends left side output as input to left |
| `>` | Redirect output |
| `>>` | Append output |
| `<` | Take input from a file |
| `2>` | Redirect errors |
| `&>` | Redirect output and error i.e file descriptors |

## 6. Process Management

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `ps` | Display current process |
| `ps -ef` | Full process listing |
| `ps -u` | Process of a user |
| `ps -p PID` | Display specific process through PID |
| `ps -o` | Display specific output columns |
| `top` | Live processes monitoring |
| `htop` | Give the user-friendly summary of top |
| `kill` | Gives the signal |
| `kill -9` | Forceful termination |
| `pkill` | Kill process by name |
| `pkill -9` | |
| `pgrep` | Find process IDs by name or pattern |
| `jobs` | |

## 7. Disk and Memory Management

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `df -h` | Check disk space |
| `du -h` | Directory sizes |
| `du -sh` | Directory sizes, s adds summary to it |
| `free -h` | Checks RAM usage |

## 8. System Information

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `uname -a -m` | Displays system information, all information, check architecture |
| `whoami` | Display current username |
| `lscpu` | Display CPU information |
| `lspci` | Display PCI devices |
| `id` | Display user IDs and group IDs |
| `groups` | Display user groups |
| `date` | Display date |
| `uptime` | Display system uptime |
| `hostname` | Display system hostname |

## 9. Networking

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `ping google.com` | Tests Google network connectivity |
| `ping -c 4 google.com` | Send 4 packets |
| `ip addr` | Display IP addresses |
| `ip route` | Display routing table |
| `ifconfig` | Display network interfaces |
| `ss -tuln` | Display listening UDP and TCP ports |
| `ss -tulpn` | Display listening ports and processes |
| `ssh` | Connects to remote server |
| `hostname -I` | Display local IP address |
| `nslookup google.com` | Find IP addresses of domain |

## 10. Package Management

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `sudo apt update` | Updates packages |
| `sudo apt upgrade` | Upgrades packages |
| `sudo apt install package` | Install software |
| `sudo apt remove package` | Remove software |
| `sudo apt purge package` | Remove software and system configuration |
| `sudo apt autoremove` | Remove unusual dependencies |
| `apt search package` | Search |
| `apt show package` | Show details |

## 11. Environment Variables and Shell

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `which python3` | Locate executable |
| `echo $SHELL` | Display current shell |
| `printenv` | Display environment variables |

